## Art slots: the road up to Highbank and the Tower scene (Claude, 2026-10-26, placeholder factory lane S; Preston:
## "they just appear in the town afterwards ... a scene walking through a forest or something where they are
## talking"). The road is a side-on strip (scripts/story/route_scene.gd, scenes/road_to_highbank.tscn): parallax
## layers from the sky to the near ferns, three props on the trail, Highbank and the Wayline Tower far off on the
## horizon, and the held view from the rise. story.backdrop.tower_sky is the sky behind the Tower while the camera
## pans up it (scripts/story/tower_reveal.gd).
## Rows use the fields of docs/design/placeholder-factory-2026-10-26/03-spec-format.md 2.1. Every placeholder is
## coded in route_scene.gd (paint_slot) or tower_reveal.gd (paint_sky) at exactly the slot's size. The scene draws
## each layer through ArtSlots.texture(), so a file dropped at the exact size replaces the placeholder and nothing else.
## Aerial perspective (Preston, 2026-10-26: Highbank and the Tower faded with distance): paint every layer in full
## colour with less detail the farther it is; the scene mixes each far layer toward the sky's haze itself (HAZE in
## route_scene.gd), so a file is not hazed twice. Parallax speeds and placements live in RouteScene.ROUTES.
## All names are working labels.

